,0.35,2.03,-0.96,-0.82,0.62,0.15,-1.37,-1.08,-1.1,1.3,-0.76],"paragraph":"Mar–May in San Francisco has warmed by about 0.2 °C per decade since 1951, roughly 1.3 °C in all. There is a clear El Niño signal on temperature: after El Niño conditions in the preceding fall, Mar–May tends to run warmer. With this year's strong El Niño, that push is about 50% of a normal year-to-year swing, roughly as much warmth as 23 years of the long-term trend. Rainfall and humidity show no clear trend or El Niño link. For Mar–May 2027, a warmer-than-normal season has about even odds (about 55%), about 0.7 °C above the 1991–2020 average. The El Niño expected for Sep–Nov 2026 is stronger than any in the record used here, so the outlook extends the historical relationship beyond what has been observed. This outlook is based on the El Niño strength expected for Sep–Nov 2026 and will be updated when it is observed in early December.","variables":{"temperature":{"normal_1991_2020":13.771,"trend_per_decade":0.1794,"trend_p":0.0,"trend_total_since_1951":1.3459,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.226,"enso_p":0.0206,"confidence":"Clear","survives_fdr":false,"fraction_explained":0.0723,"intrinsic_sd":0.759,"effect_this_season":0.4073,"effect_ratio":0.5366,"size":"Substantial","size_typical_el_nino":"Noticeable","once_every_n_years_without_el_nino":3,"expected_anomaly_2027":0.7061,"forecast_mean":14.4772,"forecast_sd":0.8113,"p_below":0.0574,"p_near":0.4044,"p_above":0.5382,"forecast_words":"About even odds (54%): a warmer-than-normal season","within_record":false,"enso_effect_shrunk_per_degC":0.161,"shrink_factor":0.7123,"effect_this_season_raw":0.5718,"trend_part_2027":0.2988,"roni_upper_within_record":false,"years_of_warming_equivalent":22.6974,"percentiles":{"p05":{"trend_per_decade":0.224,"trend_p":0.0006,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.2745,"enso_p":0.0487,"confidence":"Clear","shift_this_season":0.6944,"lines_cross":false},"p50":{"trend_per_decade":0.1959,"trend_p":0.0,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.2454,"enso_p":